#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""glaeda-mini-setup: take a fresh cmux Mac mini from unboxed to build-host ready.

    glaeda-mini-setup                      plan: preflight + what --apply would change
    glaeda-mini-setup --apply              install tools, LaunchAgents, user-level defaults
    glaeda-mini-setup --uninstall          plan removal of what --apply installed
    glaeda-mini-setup --uninstall --apply  remove it
    glaeda-mini-setup --cmux-root ~/Projects/cmux   also run the read-only fleet bootstrap
    glaeda-mini-setup --hygiene-only --apply        any Mac (a laptop, a Studio): only the
                                                    disk and worktree hygiene tools and agents
    glaeda-mini-setup --runner [--apply]   GitHub Actions runner for manaflow-ai/cmux
                                           (scripts/glaeda-cmux-runner, docs/CMUX_MINI_RUNNER.md)

First, on a fresh Mac: install the Command Line Tools (xcode-select --install) and, ideally,
Homebrew. Until the Command Line Tools exist, /usr/bin/python3 and /usr/bin/git are stubs that
only open an install dialog, so this command cannot run with them. Run it with a Homebrew
python3 or after the Command Line Tools are installed.

Planning performs no side effects. --apply is idempotent: a second run reports every
action as unchanged. Everything it touches is under $HOME and owned by the current user.
Nothing here uses sudo, changes system or security settings, installs Xcode, accepts a
licence, registers a runner, or reads a token. Steps that need any of those are printed
as operator steps instead. The one exception is the explicit --runner mode, which registers a
GitHub Actions runner and is documented in docs/CMUX_MINI_RUNNER.md.

What --apply installs (templated for the current user):
    ~/.local/bin/glaeda-disk                   from scripts/glaeda-disk
    ~/.local/bin/glaeda-procs                  from scripts/glaeda-procs (why the Mac lags; --apply ends leaked fixtures)
    ~/.local/bin/glaeda-local-guard            from scripts/glaeda-local-guard (stops test and build runs orphaned by an
                                               agent session on a hygiene-only Mac; a no-op on build hosts)
    ~/.local/bin/glaeda-worktree-reclaim       built from src/bin/glaeda-worktree-reclaim.rs
    ~/.local/bin/glaeda-worktree-reclaim-all   from scripts/glaeda-worktree-reclaim-all
    ~/.local/bin/glaeda-fleet-cas-prune        from scripts/glaeda-fleet-cas-prune (a no-op without fleet-cas)
    ~/.local/bin/glaeda-seed-prefetch          from scripts/glaeda-seed-prefetch (a no-op off an owned cmux runner)
    ~/.local/bin/glaeda-lan-fetch              from scripts/glaeda-lan-fetch (compiled products from LAN peers; a
                                               miss without a mesh config). CI calls a root-owned copy at
                                               LAN_FETCH_ROOT_COPY, which needs sudo: an operator step
    ~/.local/bin/glaeda-idle-warm              from scripts/glaeda-idle-warm (builds main into a far kept root while an
                                               owned cmux mini is idle; a no-op anywhere else)
    ~/.local/bin/glaeda-mini-health            from scripts/glaeda-mini-health (finds what stops a runner mini, heals what
                                               the runner user can, reports the rest for ci-dash; a no-op off a runner)
    ~/.local/bin/glaeda-update                 from scripts/glaeda-update (hourly over-the-air updates)
    ~/.local/bin/glaeda-gh                     from scripts/glaeda-gh (shared GitHub CI watcher, the one poller)
    ~/.claude/skills/github-ci-wait/SKILL.md    from skills/github-ci-wait: tells agent sessions to wait with glaeda-gh
    ~/.config/glaeda/update.json               its release ring, written once (--ota-ring canary|stable)
    ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.teamleaderleo.glaeda.{disk-pressure,disk-dedupe,worktree-reclaim,fleet-cas-prune,seed-prefetch,lan-fetch,
                                  idle-warm,mini-health,local-guard,update,gh-watch}.plist
    build-host directories and three git defaults, each set only when unset
    python@3.13 from Homebrew, only when no Python 3.13+ exists and this user owns Homebrew

glaeda-mini-enroll needs Python 3.13+ (accept-local uses os.waitid). Setup looks for it the way
enroll does and is not ready without it, so a missing interpreter shows up here, not 13 minutes
into enrollment. When Homebrew belongs to another account, the fix is printed instead.

--hygiene-only is for machines that are not fleet build hosts, such as personal MacBooks.
It installs the tools and LaunchAgents above and nothing else: no build-host
directories, no git defaults, no operator steps, no fleet bootstrap. Only a missing python3
blocks it; build-host checks (free disk, Xcode pin, hardware) are reported, not enforced,
so a nearly full laptop can still install the tool that frees it. After that, glaeda-update
keeps every host on its release ring (docs/GLAEDA_OTA.md): each hour it runs this command from
the newest release on the ring, then rolls back if the new tools do not run.

Linux (Big Red, owned Linux machines, Linux VMs on the fleet) gets the hygiene profile, the
only one written for it so far, with or without the flag. It installs the same tools and
the systemd user units in ops/systemd (glaeda-disk-pressure, glaeda-worktree-reclaim and
glaeda-update, each a service and a timer, and the long-running glaeda-gh service) into
~/.config/systemd/user, reloads the user manager and enables the timers and glaeda-gh. There is no disk-dedupe unit (it watches Xcode DerivedData). A missing systemd user
manager blocks; lingering off is reported, since timers then stop at logout.

Machine enrollment stays with scripts/glaeda-mini-enroll, which drives
scripts/cmux-fleet-bootstrap-macos and scripts/cmux_fleet.py (docs/CMUX_FLEET_ENROLLMENT.md).
This command only runs that bootstrap read-only and records its verdict. The receipt lands in ~/.local/state/glaeda/mini-setup/receipt.json.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import contextlib
import datetime
import functools
import hashlib
import json
import os
import platform
import plistlib
import pwd
import re
import shutil
import stat
import subprocess
import sys
import time
from pathlib import Path
from typing import Any

SCHEMA = "glaeda-mini-setup/v1"
SCRIPT_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
REPO = SCRIPT_DIR.parent
sys.path.insert(0, os.fspath(SCRIPT_DIR))
import cmux_fleet_bootstrap as fleet  # noqa: E402  (read-only helpers; importing does not alter its generation)

# The machines this was written for. A different host still works; preflight says how it differs.
TARGET = {"machine": "Mac mini", "chip": "Apple M4 Pro", "cpus": 14, "memoryGiB": 48}
CMUX_XCODE_APP = "/Applications/Xcode_26.6.app"  # vars.CMUX_CI_XCODE_APP_PR, which the persistent producer reads first
MIN_FREE_GIB = fleet.default_min_free_gib("macos")  # one build slot, as the fleet bootstrap
SUPPORTED_MACOS = {15, 26}
LABEL_PREFIX = "com.teamleaderleo.glaeda."
GIT_DEFAULTS = (
    ("core.untrackedCache", "true"),  # faster status on large checkouts such as cmux
    ("fetch.parallel", "0"),  # parallel fetches, sized by git
    ("submodule.fetchJobs", "0"),  # cmux has submodules; fetch them in parallel
)
DARWIN_REQUIRED = True
# The platform this run sets up. Linux supports the hygiene profile only.
HOST_PLATFORM = "linux" if platform.system() == "Linux" else "macos"
# Linux: the systemd user units installed verbatim from ops/systemd, which stay their one definition.
SYSTEMD_UNITS_DIR = REPO / "ops/systemd"
LINUX_UNITS = (
    "glaeda-disk-pressure.service",
    "glaeda-disk-pressure.timer",
    "glaeda-worktree-reclaim.service",
    "glaeda-worktree-reclaim.timer",
    "glaeda-update.service",
    "glaeda-update.timer",
    "glaeda-gh.service",
)
# long-running Linux services with no timer: enabled and started themselves
DAEMON_UNITS = frozenset({"glaeda-gh.service"})
# the Claude Code skill installed beside the tools
SKILL_SOURCE = REPO / "skills/github-ci-wait/SKILL.md"
# glaeda-update runs this command from a release; it sets this so setup never unloads the job running it
UPDATE_ENV = "GLAEDA_UPDATE_RUNNING"
OTA_RINGS = ("canary", "stable")
# with --hygiene-only, only these preflight failures block: the agents run python3, and on
# Linux the timers need a systemd user manager
HYGIENE_BLOCKING = frozenset({"python", "systemdUser"})
RUN_TIMEOUT = 20
ENROLL_PYTHON_FORMULA = "python@3.13"
# git before 2.55 has a `git maintenance` bug that eats memory; hosts ran with maintenance.auto off
# because of it, which let duplicate packs pile up (14 GiB in one cmux checkout on 2026-09-25)
MIN_GIT = (2, 55)
GIT_CANDIDATES = ("/opt/homebrew/bin/git", "/usr/local/bin/git", "/usr/bin/git")
# glaeda-update waits 30 minutes for this whole command; the git step must fit well inside that
GIT_BREW_TIMEOUT = 600
BREW_TIMEOUT = 1800


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- small helpers


def sha256_bytes(data: bytes) -> str:
    return "sha256:" + hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest()


def sha256_file(path: Path) -> str | None:
    try:
        return sha256_bytes(path.read_bytes())
    except OSError:
        return None


def run(argv: list[str], timeout: int = RUN_TIMEOUT, env: dict[str, str] | None = None) -> tuple[int, str]:
    """Run a read-only probe. Never raises; a missing tool is (127, "")."""
    try:
        result = subprocess.run(
            argv, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,
            text=True, timeout=timeout, env=env, check=False,
        )
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return 127, ""
    return result.returncode, result.stdout.strip()[:16384]


def which(name: str, extra: tuple[str, ...] = ()) -> str | None:
    found = shutil.which(name)
    if found:
        return found
    for candidate in extra:
        if os.access(candidate, os.X_OK):
            return candidate
    return None


class Context:
    def __init__(self, home: Path, apply: bool, python: str | None, skip_launchctl: bool,
                 reclaim_binary: Path | None, cmux_root: Path | None, glaeda_bin: Path | None,
                 xcode_app: str, min_free_gib: int, hygiene_only: bool = False,
                 platform_name: str | None = None, ota_ring: str | None = None) -> None:
        self.home = home
        self.platform = platform_name or HOST_PLATFORM
        self.hygiene_only = hygiene_only
        self.apply = apply
        self.uid = os.getuid()
        self.real_home = Path(pwd.getpwuid(self.uid).pw_dir)
        # A fake HOME (tests, rehearsals) must never reach the real launchd session.
        self.sandbox = os.path.realpath(home) != os.path.realpath(self.real_home)
        self.skip_launchctl = skip_launchctl or self.sandbox
        self.python = python or pick_python()
        self.reclaim_binary = reclaim_binary
        self.cmux_root = cmux_root
        self.glaeda_bin = glaeda_bin or home / ".local/share/glaeda/cmux-fleet/glaeda"
        self.xcode_app = xcode_app
        self.min_free_gib = min_free_gib
        self.bin = home / ".local/bin"
        linux = self.platform == "linux"
        # LaunchAgents on macOS; systemd user units on Linux
        self.agents = home / (".config/systemd/user" if linux else "Library/LaunchAgents")
        # the reclaim unit appends to ~/.local/state/glaeda-worktree-reclaim.jsonl
        self.logs = home / (".local/state" if linux else "Library/Logs")
        self.derived_data = home / "Library/Developer/Xcode/DerivedData"
        self.cache_root = home / ".cache/glaeda/cmux-native-cache"
        self.state = home / ".local/state/glaeda/mini-setup"
        self.receipt_path = self.state / "receipt.json"
        self.ota_ring = ota_ring
        self.update_config = home / ".config/glaeda/update.json"

    def show(self, path: Path | str) -> str:
        text = os.fspath(path)
        home = os.fspath(self.home)
        return "~" + text[len(home):] if text == home or text.startswith(home + "/") else text

    def git_env(self) -> dict[str, str]:
        return {
            "HOME": os.fspath(self.home),
            "XDG_CONFIG_HOME": os.fspath(self.home / ".config"),
            "PATH": os.environ.get("PATH", "/usr/bin:/bin"),
            "LC_ALL": "C",
        }


def pick_python() -> str | None:
    """The interpreter the glaeda-disk LaunchAgents run.

    /usr/bin/python3 is a stub that opens an install dialog until the Command Line Tools or
    an Xcode exist, so it only counts once one does. The fleet's Xcode is a versioned app
    such as Xcode_26.6.app, not only Xcode.app.
    """
    if HOST_PLATFORM == "linux":
        # The units run glaeda-disk through its `env python3` shebang with systemd's default PATH,
        # so only interpreters there count; a pyenv shim on the login PATH would not be found.
        for candidate in ("/usr/local/bin/python3", "/usr/bin/python3"):
            if os.access(candidate, os.X_OK):
                return candidate
        return None
    for candidate in ("/opt/homebrew/bin/python3", "/usr/local/bin/python3"):
        if os.access(candidate, os.X_OK):
            return candidate
    if Path("/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/python3").exists() or any(
        Path("/Applications").glob("Xcode*.app")
    ):
        return "/usr/bin/python3"
    return None


@functools.lru_cache(maxsize=None)
def apple_python(platform_name: str = HOST_PLATFORM) -> str | None:
    """/usr/bin/python3 once it is real (Command Line Tools or an Xcode), else None.

    macOS Local Network Privacy refuses LAN connections from a LaunchAgent whose program is not Apple's,
    children included (2026-09-25: a Homebrew python3 agent and its /usr/bin/ssh got "No route to host").
    The seed prefetch agent streams seeds from the trusted seeder over the LAN, so it runs Apple's python3.
    It must also run: a broken xcode-select or an unaccepted Xcode licence makes /usr/bin/python3 fail,
    and then the agent keeps the other interpreter (losing only the LAN step, not the prefetch).
    """
    if platform_name == "linux":
        return None
    if not (Path("/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/python3").exists() or any(
        Path("/Applications").glob("Xcode*.app")
    )):
        return None
    try:
        probe = subprocess.run(["/usr/bin/python3", "-I", "-c", "pass"], stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,
                               capture_output=True, timeout=10)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return None
    return "/usr/bin/python3" if probe.returncode == 0 else None


_ENROLL: Any = None


def enroll_module() -> Any:
    """scripts/glaeda-mini-enroll, loaded once, so setup and enroll pick the same interpreter."""
    global _ENROLL
    if _ENROLL is None:
        import importlib.machinery
        import importlib.util

        loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader("glaeda_mini_enroll", os.fspath(SCRIPT_DIR / "glaeda-mini-enroll"))
        spec = importlib.util.spec_from_loader("glaeda_mini_enroll", loader)
        module = sys.modules.get("glaeda_mini_enroll")
        if module is None:
            module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
            sys.modules["glaeda_mini_enroll"] = module  # its dataclasses look themselves up here
            loader.exec_module(module)
        _ENROLL = module
    return _ENROLL


def enroll_python(ctx: Context) -> str | None:
    """The Python 3.13+ glaeda-mini-enroll would pick for this HOME, or None."""
    return enroll_module().pick_python(None, ctx.home)


def owned_brew() -> str | None:
    """brew, when this user owns it. Shared minis often have another account's Homebrew.

    Ownership, not write access: the installer makes Cellar group-writable for admin, and
    another admin installing into it leaves the owner with files it does not own.
    """
    brew = which("brew", ("/opt/homebrew/bin/brew", "/usr/local/bin/brew"))
    if brew is None:
        return None
    prefix = Path(brew).parent.parent  # /opt/homebrew, or /usr/local on Intel (root-owned itself)
    for mark in (prefix / "Cellar", prefix / "bin"):
        try:
            return brew if mark.stat().st_uid == os.getuid() else None
        except OSError:
            continue
    return None


def brew_allowed(ctx: Context) -> bool:
    """A sandbox HOME (tests, rehearsals) must never reach the real Homebrew."""
    return not ctx.sandbox


def git_version(git: str) -> tuple[int, ...] | None:
    code, out = run([git, "--version"])
    found = re.search(r"git version (\d+)\.(\d+)(?:\.(\d+))?", out) if code == 0 else None
    return tuple(int(x) for x in found.groups() if x is not None) if found else None


def newest_git() -> tuple[str | None, tuple[int, ...] | None]:
    """The newest git among PATH and the usual install locations."""
    best: tuple[str | None, tuple[int, ...] | None] = (None, None)
    for git in dict.fromkeys(g for g in (shutil.which("git"), *GIT_CANDIDATES) if g and os.access(g, os.X_OK)):
        version = git_version(git)
        if version and (best[1] is None or version > best[1]):
            best = (git, version)
    return best


def plan_git(ctx: Context) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """git >= 2.55 on every host; Homebrew installs it when this user owns Homebrew."""
    need = ".".join(map(str, MIN_GIT))
    act: dict[str, Any] = {"kind": "gitpkg", "key": f"git>={need}", "formula": "git"}
    git, version = newest_git()
    shown = f"{git} {'.'.join(map(str, version))}" if version else "none"
    if version and version >= MIN_GIT:
        on_path = shutil.which("git")
        path_version = git_version(on_path) if on_path else None
        note = "" if not path_version or path_version >= MIN_GIT else (
            f"PATH resolves {on_path} {'.'.join(map(str, path_version))}: put {Path(git).parent} first")
        return {**act, "state": "unchanged", "value": shown, "note": note}
    if ctx.platform == "linux":
        return {**act, "state": "blocked", "value": shown,
                "note": f"git {need}+ fixes a git maintenance memory bug: sudo add-apt-repository ppa:git-core/ppa "
                        "&& sudo apt install git"}
    brew = owned_brew()
    if brew and not brew_allowed(ctx):
        return {**act, "state": "blocked", "value": shown, "note": "brew install git is not run with a sandbox HOME"}
    if brew:
        return {**act, "state": "create", "value": shown, "brew": brew,
                "note": f"brew install git: git {need}+ fixes a git maintenance memory bug"}
    return {**act, "state": "blocked", "value": shown,
            "note": f"git {need}+ fixes a git maintenance memory bug: the Homebrew owner runs brew install git"}


def brew_install(brew: str, formula: str, verb: str = "install", timeout: int = BREW_TIMEOUT,
                 no_auto_update: bool = False) -> tuple[int, str]:
    env = {**os.environ, "HOMEBREW_NO_AUTO_UPDATE": "1"} if no_auto_update else None
    try:
        result = subprocess.run([brew, verb, formula], stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=subprocess.PIPE,
                                stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, text=True, timeout=timeout, check=False, env=env)
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        return 1, f"brew {verb} {formula} timed out after {timeout} s"
    except OSError as error:
        return 1, str(error)
    return result.returncode, result.stdout


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- preflight (read-only)


def check(ok: bool | None, value: object, note: str = "", blocking: bool = False) -> dict[str, Any]:
    level = "ok" if ok else ("info" if ok is None else ("block" if blocking else "warn"))
    return {"level": level, "value": value, "note": note}


def command_line_tools_check(present: bool, version: str | None, xcode_selected_and_usable: bool) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """A selected, licensed Xcode already backs /usr/bin/git, python3 and xcrun, so the
    Command Line Tools block only a Mac that has neither."""
    if present:
        return check(True, version or "present")
    if xcode_selected_and_usable:
        return check(None, "missing", "not needed: the selected Xcode provides git and xcrun")
    return check(False, "missing", "xcode-select --install", True)


def xcode_apps() -> list[dict[str, str]]:
    apps = []
    for app in sorted(Path("/Applications").glob("Xcode*.app")):
        try:
            with (app / "Contents/Info.plist").open("rb") as stream:
                info = plistlib.load(stream)
            apps.append({"path": os.fspath(app), "version": str(info.get("CFBundleShortVersionString", "?"))})
        except (OSError, plistlib.InvalidFileException):
            apps.append({"path": os.fspath(app), "version": "unreadable"})
    return apps


def hardware() -> dict[str, Any]:
    code, raw = run(["/usr/sbin/system_profiler", "SPHardwareDataType", "-json"], timeout=30)
    info: dict[str, Any] = {}
    if code == 0:
        try:
            info = json.loads(raw)["SPHardwareDataType"][0]
        except (ValueError, KeyError, IndexError):
            info = {}
    _, chip = run(["/usr/sbin/sysctl", "-n", "machdep.cpu.brand_string"])
    _, model = run(["/usr/sbin/sysctl", "-n", "hw.model"])
    _, mem = run(["/usr/sbin/sysctl", "-n", "hw.memsize"])
    # Serial numbers, UUIDs and activation-lock state are deliberately not kept.
    return {
        "machine": info.get("machine_name") or "unknown",
        "model": info.get("machine_model") or model or "unknown",
        "chip": info.get("chip_type") or chip or "unknown",
        "cpus": os.cpu_count() or 0,
        "memoryGiB": int(mem) // (1024**3) if mem.isdigit() else 0,
        "arch": platform.machine(),
    }


def tailscale() -> dict[str, Any]:
    binary = which("tailscale", ("/Applications/Tailscale.app/Contents/MacOS/Tailscale",
                                 "/opt/homebrew/bin/tailscale", "/usr/local/bin/tailscale"))
    if binary is None:
        return {"installed": False}
    code, raw = run([binary, "status", "--json", "--peers=false"])
    out: dict[str, Any] = {"installed": True, "running": False}
    try:
        doc = json.loads(raw) if code == 0 else {}
    except ValueError:
        doc = {}
    self_node = doc.get("Self") or {}
    if doc:
        out.update({
            "running": doc.get("BackendState") == "Running",
            "backendState": doc.get("BackendState"),
            "hostname": self_node.get("HostName"),
            "dnsName": (self_node.get("DNSName") or "").rstrip(".") or None,
        })
    return out


def power() -> dict[str, Any]:
    code, raw = run(["/usr/bin/pmset", "-g", "custom"])
    if code != 0:
        return {"readable": False}
    autorestart = re.search(r"^\s*autorestart\s+(\d+)", raw, re.MULTILINE)
    womp = re.search(r"AC Power:(?:.|\n)*?^\s*womp\s+(\d+)", raw, re.MULTILINE)
    return {
        "readable": True,
        "acSleepDisabled": fleet.mac_sleep_disabled_on_ac(raw),
        "wakeOnNetwork": bool(womp and womp.group(1) == "1"),
        # Only desktops report autorestart; a laptop has no such key.
        "autoRestart": None if autorestart is None else autorestart.group(1) == "1",
    }


def preflight(ctx: Context) -> dict[str, Any]:
    return preflight_linux(ctx) if ctx.platform == "linux" else preflight_macos(ctx)


def systemctl() -> str:
    return which("systemctl", ("/usr/bin/systemctl", "/bin/systemctl")) or "/usr/bin/systemctl"


def os_release_name() -> str:
    try:
        for line in Path("/etc/os-release").read_text().splitlines():
            if line.startswith("PRETTY_NAME="):
                return line.split("=", 1)[1].strip().strip('"')
    except OSError:
        pass
    return "Linux"


def preflight_linux(ctx: Context) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """The hygiene profile's needs on Linux: a systemd user manager, python3, and cargo."""
    checks: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {}
    checks["linux"] = check(True, f"{os_release_name()} ({platform.machine()})")
    if ctx.skip_launchctl:  # sandbox HOME or --skip-systemctl: systemctl is never called
        checks["systemdUser"] = check(None, "not checked (systemctl skipped)")
    else:
        code, _ = run([systemctl(), "--user", "show-environment"])
        checks["systemdUser"] = check(
            code == 0, "available" if code == 0 else "unavailable",
            "" if code == 0 else "the timers need a systemd user manager: systemctl --user must work "
            "(log in directly, or set XDG_RUNTIME_DIR when using su or sudo -u)", True)
    user = pwd.getpwuid(ctx.uid).pw_name
    code, out = run(["loginctl", "show-user", user, "--property", "Linger", "--value"])
    linger = code == 0 and out.strip() == "yes"
    checks["linger"] = check(linger, "yes" if linger else (out.strip() or "unknown"),
                             "" if linger else f"timers stop when {user} logs out until: sudo loginctl enable-linger {user}")
    checks["python"] = check(ctx.python is not None, ctx.python or "missing",
                             "" if ctx.python else "glaeda-disk needs python3 on systemd's PATH (/usr/bin)", True)
    cargo = find_cargo(ctx)
    checks["cargo"] = check(cargo is not None or ctx.reclaim_binary is not None,
                            cargo or ("--reclaim-binary" if ctx.reclaim_binary else "missing"),
                            "" if cargo or ctx.reclaim_binary else "glaeda-worktree-reclaim is built with cargo (rustup)")
    free = fleet.disk_free_gib(ctx.home)
    checks["diskFree"] = check(free >= ctx.min_free_gib, f"{free} GiB", f"need {ctx.min_free_gib} GiB", True)
    ts = tailscale()
    checks["tailscale"] = check(ts.get("running", False),
                                ts.get("dnsName") or ts.get("hostname") or ("not installed" if not ts["installed"] else ts.get("backendState") or "not running"))
    return {
        "checks": checks,
        "hardware": {"arch": platform.machine(), "cpus": os.cpu_count() or 0},
        "tailscale": ts,
        "power": {"readable": False},
        "xcode": {"apps": [], "selected": "none", "licenceNeeded": False},
        "blocking": sorted(name for name, c in checks.items() if c["level"] == "block"),
    }


def preflight_macos(ctx: Context) -> dict[str, Any]:
    checks: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {}
    version = platform.mac_ver()[0]
    major = int(version.split(".")[0]) if version else 0
    checks["macos"] = check(major in SUPPORTED_MACOS, version or "unknown",
                            "" if major in SUPPORTED_MACOS else "fleet bootstrap accepts macOS 15 or 26", True)
    hw = hardware()
    checks["appleSilicon"] = check(hw["arch"] == "arm64", hw["arch"], "", True)
    is_mini = hw["machine"] == TARGET["machine"]
    checks["macMini"] = check(is_mini, f'{hw["machine"]} ({hw["model"]})',
                              "" if is_mini else "not a Mac mini; setup still works")
    target = hw["chip"] == TARGET["chip"] and hw["cpus"] >= TARGET["cpus"] and hw["memoryGiB"] >= TARGET["memoryGiB"]
    checks["hardware"] = check(target, f'{hw["chip"]}, {hw["cpus"]} cores, {hw["memoryGiB"]} GiB',
                               "" if target else "differs from the M4 Pro 14-core 48 GB target")
    checks["buildLargeClass"] = check(
        fleet.hardware_class_ready("macos", "cmux-mac-build-large", hw["cpus"], hw["memoryGiB"]),
        "cmux-mac-build-large", "", True)

    clt = Path("/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools")
    _, clt_pkg = run(["/usr/sbin/pkgutil", "--pkg-info=com.apple.pkg.CLTools_Executables"])
    clt_version = re.search(r"^version:\s*(\S+)", clt_pkg, re.MULTILINE)
    apps = xcode_apps()
    code, selected = run(["/usr/bin/xcode-select", "-p"])
    selected = selected if code == 0 else "none"
    xcode_code, xcode_version = run(["/usr/bin/xcrun", "xcodebuild", "-version"]) if apps else (1, "")
    licence_needed = "license" in xcode_version.lower()
    version_match = re.search(r"^Xcode\s+(\S+)", xcode_version, re.MULTILINE)
    checks["commandLineTools"] = command_line_tools_check(
        clt.is_dir(), clt_version.group(1) if clt_version else None,
        selected.startswith("/Applications/Xcode") and xcode_code == 0 and not licence_needed)
    checks["xcode"] = check(bool(apps), ", ".join(f'{Path(a["path"]).name} {a["version"]}' for a in apps) or "none",
                            "" if apps else "install Xcode (operator)", True)
    checks["xcodeSelected"] = check(selected.startswith("/Applications/Xcode"), selected,
                                    "" if selected.startswith("/Applications/Xcode") else "points at Command Line Tools, not Xcode")
    checks["xcodeUsable"] = check(xcode_code == 0 and not licence_needed,
                                  version_match.group(1) if version_match else ("licence not accepted" if licence_needed else "unavailable"),
                                  "sudo xcodebuild -license accept" if licence_needed else "")
    has_cmux_xcode = any(a["path"] == ctx.xcode_app for a in apps)
    checks["cmuxXcodePin"] = check(has_cmux_xcode, ctx.xcode_app, "" if has_cmux_xcode else "cmux CI expects this exact app")

    free = fleet.disk_free_gib(ctx.home)
    checks["diskFree"] = check(free >= ctx.min_free_gib, f"{free} GiB", f"need {ctx.min_free_gib} GiB", True)
    ts = tailscale()
    checks["tailscale"] = check(ts.get("running", False),
                                ts.get("dnsName") or ts.get("hostname") or ("not installed" if not ts["installed"] else ts.get("backendState") or "not running"))
    brew = which("brew", ("/opt/homebrew/bin/brew",))
    checks["homebrew"] = check(brew is not None, brew or "missing")
    checks["python"] = check(ctx.python is not None, ctx.python or "missing",
                             "" if ctx.python else "LaunchAgents need python3 (Homebrew or Command Line Tools)", True)
    missing = fleet.missing_workload_tools(fleet.MACOS_WORKLOAD_TOOLS)
    checks["workloadToolPath"] = check(not missing, "all present" if not missing else "missing: " + ",".join(missing),
                                       "" if not missing else "cmux ./scripts/setup.sh installs these")
    pw = power()
    checks["power"] = check(pw.get("acSleepDisabled"), "AC sleep off" if pw.get("acSleepDisabled") else "AC sleep on",
                            "" if pw.get("acSleepDisabled") else "sudo pmset, see operator steps")
    blocking = sorted(name for name, c in checks.items() if c["level"] == "block")
    return {
        "checks": checks,
        "hardware": hw,
        "tailscale": ts,
        "power": pw,
        "xcode": {"apps": apps, "selected": selected, "licenceNeeded": licence_needed},
        "blocking": blocking,
    }


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- desired state


def agent_plists(ctx: Context) -> dict[str, dict[str, Any]]:
    """The LaunchAgents for this user: disk hygiene as hand-installed on Air Blue, plus the fleet-cas pruner."""
    disk = os.fspath(ctx.bin / "glaeda-disk")
    python = ctx.python or "/usr/bin/python3"
    return {
        LABEL_PREFIX + "disk-pressure": {
            "Label": LABEL_PREFIX + "disk-pressure",
            "ProgramArguments": [python, disk, "--pressure", "--apply", "--top", "0"],
            "StartInterval": 900,
            "RunAtLoad": True,
            # Not ProcessType Background: under pressure this job must still finish its lsof and free
            # space while a build fills the disk. LowPriorityIO and Nice keep it behind the build.
            "LowPriorityIO": True,
            "Nice": 10,
            "StandardOutPath": os.fspath(ctx.logs / "glaeda-disk.log"),
            "StandardErrorPath": os.fspath(ctx.logs / "glaeda-disk.err"),
        },
        LABEL_PREFIX + "disk-dedupe": {
            "Label": LABEL_PREFIX + "disk-dedupe",
            "ProgramArguments": [python, disk, "--dedupe", "--settle-minutes", "5"],
            "WatchPaths": [os.fspath(ctx.derived_data)],
            "StartInterval": 21600,
            "ThrottleInterval": 600,
            # Hashing whole DerivedData trees is never urgent: throttle CPU and I/O like taskpolicy -b.
            "ProcessType": "Background",
            "LowPriorityIO": True,
            "Nice": 10,
            "StandardOutPath": os.fspath(ctx.logs / "glaeda-disk-dedupe.log"),
            "StandardErrorPath": os.fspath(ctx.logs / "glaeda-disk-dedupe.err"),
        },
        LABEL_PREFIX + "worktree-reclaim": {
            "Label": LABEL_PREFIX + "worktree-reclaim",
            "ProgramArguments": ["/bin/bash", os.fspath(ctx.bin / "glaeda-worktree-reclaim-all"),
                                 "--apply", "--output", "json"],
            # hourly: finished work is reclaimable after an hour idle, unfinished after three days
            "StartInterval": 3600,
            "LowPriorityIO": True,
            "Nice": 10,
            "StandardOutPath": os.fspath(ctx.logs / "glaeda-worktree-reclaim.jsonl"),
            "StandardErrorPath": os.fspath(ctx.logs / "glaeda-worktree-reclaim.err"),
        },
        # Over-the-air updates (scripts/glaeda-update): hourly, installs this host's release ring and
        # rolls back when the new tools do not run.
        LABEL_PREFIX + "update": {
            "Label": LABEL_PREFIX + "update",
            "ProgramArguments": [python, os.fspath(ctx.bin / "glaeda-update"), "--apply"],
            "StartInterval": 3600,
            "ProcessType": "Background",
            "LowPriorityIO": True,
            "Nice": 10,
            "StandardOutPath": os.fspath(ctx.logs / "glaeda-update.jsonl"),
            "StandardErrorPath": os.fspath(ctx.logs / "glaeda-update.err"),
        },
        # Keeps the fleet compilation-cache node store and local Xcode CAS within budget; it exits at
        # once on a host without fleet-cas and defers while any build runs or holds the host lock.
        LABEL_PREFIX + "fleet-cas-prune": {
            "Label": LABEL_PREFIX + "fleet-cas-prune",
            "ProgramArguments": [python, os.fspath(ctx.bin / "glaeda-fleet-cas-prune"), "--apply"],
            "StartInterval": 3600,
            "ProcessType": "Background",
            "LowPriorityIO": True,
            "Nice": 10,
            "StandardOutPath": os.fspath(ctx.logs / "glaeda-fleet-cas-prune.jsonl"),
            "StandardErrorPath": os.fspath(ctx.logs / "glaeda-fleet-cas-prune.err"),
        },
        # Fetches main's newest DerivedData seed into each canonical root's local seed cache while an owned
        # cmux runner is idle (cmuxterm-hq#658); it exits at once where no owned job has run. Apple's python3,
        # so it may reach the trusted seeder on the LAN (apple_python).
        LABEL_PREFIX + "seed-prefetch": {
            "Label": LABEL_PREFIX + "seed-prefetch",
            "ProgramArguments": [apple_python(ctx.platform) or python, os.fspath(ctx.bin / "glaeda-seed-prefetch"),
                                 "--apply"],
            "StartInterval": 300,
            "ProcessType": "Background",
            "LowPriorityIO": True,
            "Nice": 10,
            "StandardOutPath": os.fspath(ctx.logs / "glaeda-seed-prefetch.jsonl"),
            "StandardErrorPath": os.fspath(ctx.logs / "glaeda-seed-prefetch.err"),
        },
        # Idle catch-up (scripts/glaeda-idle-warm): on an idle owned cmux mini whose kept build is far from main,
        # builds main's head into that root and yields to any job; it exits at once anywhere else. Not
        # ProcessType Background: its build runs only while nothing else does, and should finish fast.
        LABEL_PREFIX + "idle-warm": {
            "Label": LABEL_PREFIX + "idle-warm",
            "ProgramArguments": [python, os.fspath(ctx.bin / "glaeda-idle-warm"), "--apply"],
            # Every minute, so a main push reaches an idle root within minutes: a busy mini stops at `ps`,
            # an idle one asks GitHub for main's head (ls-remote, no API quota).
            "StartInterval": 60,
            "Nice": 5,
            "StandardOutPath": os.fspath(ctx.logs / "glaeda-idle-warm.jsonl"),
            "StandardErrorPath": os.fspath(ctx.logs / "glaeda-idle-warm.err"),
        },
        # Runner mini health (scripts/glaeda-mini-health): a locked console, display sleep, a wedged testmanagerd,
        # Tailscale down, a stopped runner agent. Heals what this user can without disturbing a job and writes the
        # report ci-dash's probe reads; it exits at once on a host without glaeda runners.
        LABEL_PREFIX + "mini-health": {
            "Label": LABEL_PREFIX + "mini-health",
            "ProgramArguments": [python, os.fspath(ctx.bin / "glaeda-mini-health"), "--apply"],
            "StartInterval": 120,
            "RunAtLoad": True,
            "ProcessType": "Background",
            "LowPriorityIO": True,
            "Nice": 10,
            "StandardOutPath": os.fspath(ctx.logs / "glaeda-mini-health.jsonl"),
            "StandardErrorPath": os.fspath(ctx.logs / "glaeda-mini-health.err"),
        },
        # Tests and builds that outlived their agent session on a personal Mac (scripts/glaeda-local-guard): every
        # 30 seconds it ends the orphaned ones. It exits at once on a build host. Not ProcessType Background:
        # it has to get CPU while the orphans it stops hold the machine.
        LABEL_PREFIX + "local-guard": {
            "Label": LABEL_PREFIX + "local-guard",
            "ProgramArguments": [python, os.fspath(ctx.bin / "glaeda-local-guard"), "--apply"],
            "StartInterval": 30,
            "RunAtLoad": True,
            "StandardOutPath": os.fspath(ctx.logs / "glaeda-local-guard.log"),
            "StandardErrorPath": os.fspath(ctx.logs / "glaeda-local-guard.err"),
        },
        # The compiled-product LAN broker (scripts/glaeda-lan-fetch serve-local): CI steps descend from
        # non-Apple processes (Runner.Listener), so Local Network Privacy keeps them off the LAN; they ask this
        # agent over a private Unix socket instead. Apple's python3 is what lets its ssh reach the peers.
        LABEL_PREFIX + "lan-fetch": {
            "Label": LABEL_PREFIX + "lan-fetch",
            "ProgramArguments": [apple_python(ctx.platform) or python, "-I", os.fspath(ctx.bin / "glaeda-lan-fetch"),
                                 "serve-local"],
            "RunAtLoad": True,
            "KeepAlive": True,
            "ThrottleInterval": 30,
            "ProcessType": "Background",
            "StandardOutPath": os.fspath(ctx.logs / "glaeda-lan-fetch.log"),
            "StandardErrorPath": os.fspath(ctx.logs / "glaeda-lan-fetch.err"),
        },
        # The shared GitHub CI watcher (scripts/glaeda-gh): the one process that polls GitHub for every
        # session on this host. It idles without API calls while nothing is watched and re-executes
        # itself when the tool is updated.
        LABEL_PREFIX + "gh-watch": {
            "Label": LABEL_PREFIX + "gh-watch",
            "ProgramArguments": [python, os.fspath(ctx.bin / "glaeda-gh"), "serve"],
            "RunAtLoad": True,
            "KeepAlive": True,
            "ThrottleInterval": 30,
            # gh (for the token) is in Homebrew, which a LaunchAgent's PATH leaves out
            "EnvironmentVariables": {"PATH": f"{ctx.bin}:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin"},
            "StandardOutPath": os.fspath(ctx.logs / "glaeda-gh.jsonl"),
            "StandardErrorPath": os.fspath(ctx.logs / "glaeda-gh.err"),
        },
    }


def agent_names(ctx: Context) -> list[str]:
    """LaunchAgent labels on macOS; systemd unit file names on Linux."""
    return list(LINUX_UNITS) if ctx.platform == "linux" else list(agent_plists(ctx))


def agent_path(ctx: Context, label: str) -> Path:
    return ctx.agents / (label if ctx.platform == "linux" else f"{label}.plist")


def agent_bytes(ctx: Context, label: str) -> bytes:
    if ctx.platform == "linux":
        return (SYSTEMD_UNITS_DIR / label).read_bytes()
    return plistlib.dumps(agent_plists(ctx)[label], sort_keys=True)


def is_disk_agent(label: str) -> bool:
    return label.startswith((LABEL_PREFIX + "disk", "glaeda-disk"))


def is_gh_agent(label: str) -> bool:
    return label == LABEL_PREFIX + "gh-watch" or label.startswith("glaeda-gh.")


def skill_path(ctx: Context) -> Path:
    return ctx.home / ".claude/skills/github-ci-wait/SKILL.md"


def is_update_agent(label: str) -> bool:
    return label == LABEL_PREFIX + "update" or label.startswith("glaeda-update.")


def update_config(ctx: Context) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """What glaeda-update reads: this host's ring and the setup flags it re-runs releases with."""
    return {
        "ring": ctx.ota_ring or "stable",
        "setupArgs": ["--hygiene-only"] if ctx.hygiene_only else [],
        "host": platform.node().split(".")[0].lower(),
        "reportStatus": (ctx.ota_ring or "stable") == "canary",
    }


def update_config_action(ctx: Context) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """Written once. A later run changes it only when --ota-ring names a different ring."""
    path = ctx.update_config
    act: dict[str, Any] = {"kind": "config", "path": os.fspath(path), "mode": "0o644"}
    try:
        current = json.loads(path.read_text())
    except FileNotFoundError:
        current = None
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return {**act, "state": "blocked", "note": "unreadable; fix or remove it"}
    if current is None:
        return {**act, "state": "create", "value": update_config(ctx)}
    if ctx.ota_ring and current.get("ring") != ctx.ota_ring:
        value = {**current, "ring": ctx.ota_ring, "reportStatus": ctx.ota_ring == "canary"}
        return {**act, "state": "update", "value": value, "previous": current.get("ring")}
    return {**act, "state": "unchanged", "value": current}


def is_reclaim_agent(label: str) -> bool:
    return label == LABEL_PREFIX + "worktree-reclaim" or label.startswith("glaeda-worktree-reclaim.")


def directories(ctx: Context) -> list[tuple[Path, int]]:
    if ctx.platform == "linux":
        return [
            (ctx.bin, 0o755),
            (ctx.agents, 0o755),
            (ctx.logs, 0o755),
            (ctx.home / "Projects", 0o755),  # glaeda-worktree-reclaim-all scans here
            (ctx.state, 0o700),
        ]
    dirs = [
        (ctx.bin, 0o755),
        (ctx.agents, 0o755),
        (ctx.logs, 0o755),
        (ctx.derived_data, 0o755),  # the dedupe agent watches it; launchd needs it to exist
        (ctx.home / "Projects", 0o755),  # glaeda-worktree-reclaim-all scans here
        (ctx.cache_root, 0o700),  # --cache-root for the cmux_macos_native_build role
        (ctx.state, 0o700),
    ]
    return [d for d in dirs if not (ctx.hygiene_only and d[0] == ctx.cache_root)]


def reclaim_source(ctx: Context) -> tuple[str, Path | None, str]:
    """Where glaeda-worktree-reclaim comes from: (mode, path, note)."""
    if ctx.reclaim_binary is not None:
        return "prebuilt", ctx.reclaim_binary, "from --reclaim-binary"
    target = Path(os.environ.get("CARGO_TARGET_DIR") or REPO / "target") / "release/glaeda-worktree-reclaim"
    cargo = find_cargo(ctx)
    if cargo:
        return "build", target, f"cargo build --locked --release --bin glaeda-worktree-reclaim ({cargo})"
    if target.is_file():
        return "prebuilt", target, "existing build; cargo not found to refresh it"
    return "blocked", None, "needs cargo (rustup) or --reclaim-binary PATH from a fleet bundle"


def launchctl_loaded(ctx: Context, label: str) -> bool | None:
    if ctx.skip_launchctl:
        return None
    code, _ = run(["/bin/launchctl", "print", f"gui/{ctx.uid}/{label}"])
    return code == 0


def agent_loaded(ctx: Context, label: str) -> bool | None:
    """Loaded in launchd, or on Linux a timer that is enabled and active. Services start from their timer."""
    if ctx.platform != "linux":
        return launchctl_loaded(ctx, label)
    if ctx.skip_launchctl or not (label.endswith(".timer") or label in DAEMON_UNITS):
        return None
    # run() merges stderr, so a warning can sit beside the answer: look for the answer's line.
    code, out = run([systemctl(), "--user", "is-enabled", label])
    enabled = code == 0 and "enabled" in out.splitlines()
    code, out = run([systemctl(), "--user", "is-active", label])
    return enabled and code == 0 and "active" in out.splitlines()


def git_get(ctx: Context, key: str) -> str | None:
    git = which("git")
    if git is None:
        return None
    code, out = run([git, "config", "--global", "--get", key], env=ctx.git_env())
    return out if code == 0 else None


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- plan


def file_action(ctx: Context, kind: str, dest: Path, data: bytes | None, mode: int, note: str = "") -> dict[str, Any]:
    current = sha256_file(dest)
    want = sha256_bytes(data) if data is not None else None
    if data is None:
        state = "blocked"
    elif current is None:
        state = "create"
    elif current == want and (dest.stat().st_mode & 0o777) == mode:
        state = "unchanged"
    else:
        state = "update"
    return {"kind": kind, "path": os.fspath(dest), "state": state, "sha256": want,
            "previousSha256": current, "mode": oct(mode), "note": note}


def plan_install(ctx: Context) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:
    actions: list[dict[str, Any]] = []
    for path, mode in directories(ctx):
        actions.append({"kind": "dir", "path": os.fspath(path),
                        "state": "unchanged" if path.is_dir() else "create", "mode": oct(mode)})
    for name in ("glaeda-disk", "glaeda-procs", "glaeda-local-guard", "glaeda-worktree-reclaim-all", "glaeda-fleet-cas-prune", "glaeda-seed-prefetch",
                 "glaeda-lan-fetch", "glaeda-idle-warm", "glaeda-mini-health",
                 "glaeda-update", "glaeda-gh"):
        act = file_action(ctx, "tool", ctx.bin / name, (SCRIPT_DIR / name).read_bytes(), 0o755)
        act["source"] = os.fspath(SCRIPT_DIR / name)
        actions.append(act)
    # a copy, not a link: the release tree it came from is replaced by the next update
    act = file_action(ctx, "tool", skill_path(ctx), SKILL_SOURCE.read_bytes(), 0o644)
    act["source"] = os.fspath(SKILL_SOURCE)
    actions.append(act)
    mode, source, note = reclaim_source(ctx)
    dest = ctx.bin / "glaeda-worktree-reclaim"
    if mode == "blocked":
        act = file_action(ctx, "tool", dest, None, 0o755, note)
        act["source"] = None
        actions.append(act)
    elif mode == "build":
        # The binary does not exist until cargo runs, so plan says build and compares afterwards.
        prior = source.read_bytes() if source is not None and source.is_file() else None
        act = file_action(ctx, "tool", dest, prior, 0o755, note)
        if prior is None:
            act["state"] = "create" if not dest.exists() else "update"
        # An unchanged binary needs no cargo run at apply time.
        act["build"] = act["state"] != "unchanged"
        act["source"] = os.fspath(source)
        actions.append(act)
    else:
        data = source.read_bytes() if source is not None and source.is_file() else None
        act = file_action(ctx, "tool", dest, data, 0o755, note)
        act["source"] = os.fspath(source) if source else None
        actions.append(act)

    reclaim_act = actions[-1]
    prior_receipt = load_receipt(ctx) or {}
    owned_files = {a.get("path"): a.get("ownedSha256") or a.get("sha256") for a in prior_receipt.get("actions", [])
                   if a.get("kind") in {"tool", "agent"} and a.get("owned")}
    for label in agent_names(ctx):
        dest = agent_path(ctx, label)
        act = file_action(ctx, "agent", dest, agent_bytes(ctx, label), 0o644)
        if ctx.platform != "linux" and act["state"] == "update":
            doc = agent_plists(ctx)[label]
            try:  # a hand-written plist with the same content is not a change
                with dest.open("rb") as stream:
                    if plistlib.load(stream) == doc:
                        act["state"] = "unchanged"
                        act["sha256"] = act["previousSha256"]
            except (OSError, plistlib.InvalidFileException, ValueError):
                pass
        if ctx.python is None and (is_disk_agent(label) or is_update_agent(label) or is_gh_agent(label)):
            act["state"], act["note"] = "blocked", "no usable python3 yet"
        if is_reclaim_agent(label) and reclaim_act["state"] == "blocked":
            act["state"], act["note"] = "blocked", "glaeda-worktree-reclaim could not be installed"
        act["label"] = label
        act["loaded"] = agent_loaded(ctx, label)
        scheduler = "systemctl" if ctx.platform == "linux" else "launchctl"
        act[scheduler] = "skipped (sandbox HOME)" if ctx.sandbox else ("skipped" if ctx.skip_launchctl else "managed")
        actions.append(act)

    actions.append(update_config_action(ctx))

    # owned: this command wrote the file (now or on an earlier run) and it is still those bytes.
    # A file that was already identical before the first install is never owned, so never removed.
    # Ownership follows the bytes on disk, not this run's outcome: a blocked or failed step
    # (missing cargo, missing --reclaim-binary) must not orphan a file an earlier run installed.
    for act in actions:
        if act["kind"] in {"tool", "agent"}:
            recorded = owned_files.get(act["path"])
            act["owned"] = recorded is not None and recorded == act.get("previousSha256")
            act["ownedSha256"] = recorded if act["owned"] else None

    # /usr/bin/git is an install-dialog stub until the Command Line Tools (or Xcode) exist.
    git_ok = which("git") is not None and (
        ctx.platform == "linux" or not DARWIN_REQUIRED or Path("/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools").exists() or bool(xcode_apps()))
    prior = load_receipt(ctx) or {}
    owned_before = {a.get("key") for a in prior.get("actions", []) if a.get("kind") == "git" and a.get("owned")}
    for key, value in () if ctx.hygiene_only else GIT_DEFAULTS:
        current = git_get(ctx, key) if git_ok else None
        if not git_ok:
            state, note = "blocked", "git needs the Command Line Tools"
        elif current is None:
            state, note = "create", ""
        elif current == value:
            state, note = "unchanged", ""
        else:
            state, note = "kept", f"already set to {current}; left alone"
        # owned: this command set the key, on this run or an earlier one, so --uninstall may unset it.
        actions.append({"kind": "git", "key": key, "value": value, "state": state, "previous": current,
                        "note": note, "owned": state == "unchanged" and key in owned_before})
    if not ctx.hygiene_only:
        actions.append(plan_enroll_python(ctx))
    actions.append(plan_git(ctx))
    return actions


def plan_enroll_python(ctx: Context) -> dict[str, Any]:
    act: dict[str, Any] = {"kind": "python", "key": "enroll-python", "formula": ENROLL_PYTHON_FORMULA}
    found = enroll_python(ctx)
    if found:
        return {**act, "state": "unchanged", "value": found, "note": ""}
    brew = owned_brew()
    if brew and not brew_allowed(ctx):
        return {**act, "state": "blocked", "value": None,
                "note": f"brew install {ENROLL_PYTHON_FORMULA} is not run with a sandbox HOME"}
    if brew:
        return {**act, "state": "create", "value": None, "brew": brew,
                "note": f"brew install {ENROLL_PYTHON_FORMULA}; glaeda-mini-enroll needs Python 3.13+"}
    return {**act, "state": "blocked", "value": None,
            "note": "glaeda-mini-enroll needs Python 3.13+: " + enroll_module().PYTHON_FIX}


def load_receipt(ctx: Context) -> dict[str, Any] | None:
    try:
        return json.loads(ctx.receipt_path.read_text())
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None


def plan_uninstall(ctx: Context) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:
    receipt = load_receipt(ctx)
    # Only files this command wrote (create or update, carried forward as "owned") are removable.
    installed = {a["path"]: a.get("ownedSha256") or a.get("sha256") for a in (receipt or {}).get("actions", [])
                 if a.get("kind") in {"tool", "agent"} and a.get("owned")}
    git_set = {a["key"]: a["value"] for a in (receipt or {}).get("actions", [])
               if a.get("kind") == "git" and a.get("owned")}
    actions: list[dict[str, Any]] = []
    if receipt is None:
        actions.append({"kind": "note", "state": "kept",
                        "note": f"no install receipt at {ctx.show(ctx.receipt_path)}; nothing is removed"})
    for label in agent_names(ctx):
        path = agent_path(ctx, label)
        actions.append({"kind": "agent", "label": label, "path": os.fspath(path),
                        "loaded": agent_loaded(ctx, label)})
    for name in ("glaeda-disk", "glaeda-procs", "glaeda-local-guard", "glaeda-worktree-reclaim", "glaeda-worktree-reclaim-all", "glaeda-fleet-cas-prune",
                 "glaeda-seed-prefetch", "glaeda-lan-fetch", "glaeda-idle-warm", "glaeda-mini-health",
                 "glaeda-update", "glaeda-gh"):
        actions.append({"kind": "tool", "path": os.fspath(ctx.bin / name)})
    actions.append({"kind": "tool", "path": os.fspath(skill_path(ctx))})
    for act in actions:
        if act["kind"] == "note":
            continue
        path = Path(act["path"])
        current = sha256_file(path)
        expected = installed.get(act["path"])
        if current is None:
            act["state"] = "absent"
        elif expected is None:
            act["state"], act["note"] = "kept", "not installed by this command"
        elif current == expected:
            act["state"] = "remove"
        else:
            act["state"], act["note"] = "kept", "changed since this command installed it"
        act["sha256"] = current
    for key, value in GIT_DEFAULTS:
        current = git_get(ctx, key)
        ours = git_set.get(key) == value
        state = "remove" if ours and current == value else ("absent" if current is None else "kept")
        actions.append({"kind": "git", "key": key, "value": current, "state": state,
                        "note": "" if ours or current is None else "not set by this command"})
    actions.append({"kind": "note", "state": "kept",
                    "note": "directories, logs, caches and any python@3.13 are left in place; remove them by hand if wanted"})
    return actions


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- apply


def write_atomic(path: Path, data: bytes, mode: int) -> None:
    stage = path.with_name(f".{path.name}.mini-setup.tmp")
    stage.write_bytes(data)
    os.chmod(stage, mode)
    os.replace(stage, path)


def backup(ctx: Context, path: Path) -> str:
    stamp = datetime.datetime.now().strftime("%Y%m%dT%H%M%S")
    dest = ctx.state / "backup" / f"{path.name}.{stamp}"
    dest.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True, mode=0o700)
    shutil.copy2(path, dest)
    return os.fspath(dest)


def launchctl(ctx: Context, *args: str) -> tuple[int, str]:
    return run(["/bin/launchctl", *args])


def bootout(ctx: Context, label: str, wait_s: float = 5.0) -> bool:
    """Unload a job and wait (bounded) until launchd no longer lists it."""
    launchctl(ctx, "bootout", f"gui/{ctx.uid}/{label}")
    deadline = time.monotonic() + wait_s
    while time.monotonic() < deadline:
        if launchctl(ctx, "print", f"gui/{ctx.uid}/{label}")[0] != 0:
            return True
        time.sleep(0.25)
    return False


def bootstrap(ctx: Context, plist: str) -> tuple[int, str]:
    """Load a job. launchd answers EIO (5) while a just-removed job is still settling; retry once."""
    code, out = launchctl(ctx, "bootstrap", f"gui/{ctx.uid}", plist)
    if code != 0 and ("Input/output error" in out or code == 5 or re.search(r"\b5:", out)):
        time.sleep(1.0)
        code, out = launchctl(ctx, "bootstrap", f"gui/{ctx.uid}", plist)
    return code, out


def apply_install(ctx: Context, actions: list[dict[str, Any]]) -> None:
    reclaim_failed = False
    for act in actions:
        kind, state = act["kind"], act["state"]
        act["applied"] = False
        if kind == "dir":
            path = Path(act["path"])
            if state == "create":
                path.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True, mode=int(act["mode"], 8))
                act["applied"] = True
            continue
        if kind == "agent" and is_reclaim_agent(act["label"]) and reclaim_failed:
            act["state"], act["note"] = "blocked", "glaeda-worktree-reclaim could not be installed"
            continue
        if kind == "tool" and act.get("build"):
            code, out = build_reclaim(ctx)
            source = Path(act["source"])
            if code != 0 or not source.is_file():
                act["state"], act["note"] = "failed", "cargo build failed: " + out[-400:]
                reclaim_failed = True
                continue
            fresh = file_action(ctx, "tool", Path(act["path"]), source.read_bytes(), 0o755, act["note"])
            act.update({k: fresh[k] for k in ("state", "sha256", "previousSha256")})
            state = act["state"]
        if kind in {"tool", "agent"} and state in {"create", "update"}:
            dest = Path(act["path"])
            if kind == "tool":
                data = Path(act["source"]).read_bytes()
            else:
                data = agent_bytes(ctx, act["label"])
            if state == "update":
                act["backup"] = backup(ctx, dest)
            dest.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)  # the skill's directory may not exist yet
            if kind == "agent" and act.get("loaded") and ctx.platform != "linux":
                if is_update_agent(act["label"]) and os.environ.get(UPDATE_ENV):
                    # unloading would kill the glaeda-update that is running this setup; launchd
                    # reads the new plist at the next login, or when setup runs by hand
                    write_atomic(Path(act["path"]), data, int(act["mode"], 8))
                    act["applied"] = act["owned"] = True
                    act["ownedSha256"] = act["sha256"]
                    act["note"] = "written; reload deferred while glaeda-update runs"
                    continue
                bootout(ctx, act["label"])
                act["loaded"] = False
            write_atomic(dest, data, int(act["mode"], 8))
            act["applied"] = act["owned"] = True
            act["ownedSha256"] = act["sha256"]
        if (kind == "agent" and ctx.platform != "linux" and state in {"create", "update", "unchanged"}
                and not ctx.skip_launchctl and not act.get("loaded")):
            code, out = bootstrap(ctx, act["path"])
            act["bootstrapped"] = code == 0
            if code != 0:
                act["note"] = ("launchctl bootstrap failed: " + out)[:400]
        if kind == "config" and state in {"create", "update"}:
            path = Path(act["path"])
            path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
            write_atomic(path, (json.dumps(act["value"], indent=1, sort_keys=True) + "\n").encode(), 0o644)
            act["applied"] = True
        if kind == "gitpkg" and state == "create":
            # bottles only, no self-update: both calls fit well inside glaeda-update's wait for setup
            code, out = brew_install(act["brew"], "git", timeout=GIT_BREW_TIMEOUT, no_auto_update=True)
            _, version = newest_git()
            if code == 0 and not (version and version >= MIN_GIT):
                # `brew install` leaves an outdated keg alone; upgrade it
                code, more = brew_install(act["brew"], "git", verb="upgrade", timeout=GIT_BREW_TIMEOUT,
                                          no_auto_update=True)
                out += more
                _, version = newest_git()
            act["applied"] = bool(version and version >= MIN_GIT)
            act["value"] = ".".join(map(str, version)) if version else None
            if not act["applied"]:
                act["state"], act["note"] = "failed", f"brew install git exited {code}: {out.strip()[-300:]}"[:400]
        if kind == "python" and state == "create":
            code, out = brew_install(act["brew"], act["formula"])
            found = enroll_python(ctx)
            act["applied"] = found is not None
            act["value"] = found
            if found is None:
                act["state"] = "failed"
                act["note"] = (f"brew install {act['formula']} exited {code} and no Python 3.13+ was found: "
                               + out.strip()[-300:])[:400]
        if kind == "git" and state == "create":
            code, out = run([which("git") or "git", "config", "--global", act["key"], act["value"]], env=ctx.git_env())
            act["applied"] = act["owned"] = code == 0
            if code != 0:
                act["state"], act["note"] = "failed", out[:400]
    if ctx.platform == "linux" and not ctx.skip_launchctl:
        activate_systemd(ctx, actions)


def activate_systemd(ctx: Context, actions: list[dict[str, Any]]) -> None:
    """Reload the user manager, then start every timer that is not running.

    A timer whose own file or whose service changed is restarted so the new definition applies.
    Any failure marks that action failed, so the receipt is not ready and the run exits 1.
    """
    agents = [a for a in actions if a["kind"] == "agent"]
    timers = [a for a in agents if (a["label"].endswith(".timer") or a["label"] in DAEMON_UNITS)
              and a["state"] in {"create", "update", "unchanged"}]
    changed = {a["label"] for a in agents if a.get("applied")}
    pending = [a for a in timers if not a.get("loaded")
               or {a["label"], a["label"].removesuffix(".timer") + ".service"} & changed]
    if not changed and not pending:
        return
    # Reload before any enable: a hand-copied unit systemd has not read yet is "not found".
    code, out = run([systemctl(), "--user", "daemon-reload"])
    if code != 0:
        for act in pending or timers:
            act["state"], act["note"] = "failed", ("systemctl --user daemon-reload failed: " + out)[:400]
        return
    for act in pending:
        steps = [["enable", "--now"]] if not act.get("loaded") else [["restart"], ["enable"]]
        for verb in steps:
            code, out = run([systemctl(), "--user", *verb, act["label"]])
            if code != 0:
                act["state"] = "failed"
                act["note"] = (f"systemctl --user {' '.join(verb)} failed: " + out)[:400]
                break
        act["enabled"] = act["state"] != "failed"


def find_cargo(ctx: Context) -> str | None:
    return which("cargo", (os.fspath(ctx.home / ".cargo/bin/cargo"), "/opt/homebrew/bin/cargo"))


def build_reclaim(ctx: Context) -> tuple[int, str]:
    cargo = find_cargo(ctx) or "cargo"
    try:
        result = subprocess.run(
            [cargo, "build", "--locked", "--release", "--bin", "glaeda-worktree-reclaim"],
            cwd=REPO, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,
            text=True, timeout=1800, check=False,
        )
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as error:
        return 1, str(error)
    return result.returncode, result.stdout


def apply_uninstall(ctx: Context, actions: list[dict[str, Any]]) -> None:
    for act in actions:
        act["applied"] = False
        if act["kind"] == "agent":
            if act["state"] == "remove" and ctx.platform == "linux" and not ctx.skip_launchctl:
                # Whatever is_enabled/is_active said: a stopped-but-enabled timer leaves a wants
                # link, and an active-but-disabled one keeps firing after its file is gone.
                verb = ["disable", "--now"] if act["label"].endswith(".timer") or act["label"] in DAEMON_UNITS else ["stop"]
                run([systemctl(), "--user", *verb, act["label"]])
            elif act.get("loaded") and act["state"] == "remove" and ctx.platform != "linux":
                bootout(ctx, act["label"])
            if act["state"] == "remove":
                Path(act["path"]).unlink()
                act["applied"] = True
        elif act["kind"] == "tool" and act["state"] == "remove":
            Path(act["path"]).unlink()
            act["applied"] = True
            if Path(act["path"]) == skill_path(ctx):
                with contextlib.suppress(OSError):  # only when empty
                    skill_path(ctx).parent.rmdir()
        elif act["kind"] == "git" and act["state"] == "remove":
            code, _ = run([which("git") or "git", "config", "--global", "--unset", act["key"]], env=ctx.git_env())
            act["applied"] = code == 0
    if (ctx.platform == "linux" and not ctx.skip_launchctl
            and any(a["kind"] == "agent" and a.get("applied") for a in actions)):
        run([systemctl(), "--user", "daemon-reload"])


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- operator steps and reserved slots


def operator_steps(ctx: Context, pre: dict[str, Any], fleet_result: dict[str, Any] | None,
                   actions: list[dict[str, Any]] = ()) -> list[dict[str, str]]:
    steps: list[dict[str, str]] = []

    def add(why: str, command: str, needs: str) -> None:
        steps.append({"why": why, "command": command, "needs": needs})

    c = pre["checks"]
    if c["commandLineTools"]["level"] not in {"ok", "info"}:
        add("Command Line Tools missing", "xcode-select --install", "human (GUI dialog)")
    if c["xcode"]["level"] != "ok" or c["cmuxXcodePin"]["level"] != "ok":
        add(f"cmux CI pins {ctx.xcode_app}", f"install Xcode at {ctx.xcode_app} (xcodes or the Apple developer site)", "human")
    if pre["xcode"]["licenceNeeded"] or c["xcodeUsable"]["level"] != "ok":
        add("Xcode licence and first-launch components", "sudo xcodebuild -license accept && sudo xcodebuild -runFirstLaunch", "sudo")
    if c["xcodeSelected"]["level"] != "ok" or (c["cmuxXcodePin"]["level"] == "ok" and pre["xcode"]["selected"] != ctx.xcode_app + "/Contents/Developer"):
        add("select the pinned Xcode", f"sudo xcode-select -s {ctx.xcode_app}", "sudo")
    power_state = pre["power"]
    if power_state.get("readable") and not power_state.get("acSleepDisabled"):
        add("unattended builds need AC sleep off (fleet check unattendedPower)", "sudo pmset -c sleep 0", "sudo")
    if power_state.get("readable") and not power_state.get("wakeOnNetwork"):
        add("wake over the network", "sudo pmset -c womp 1", "sudo")
    if power_state.get("autoRestart") is False:
        add("come back after a power cut", "sudo pmset -a autorestart 1", "sudo")
    if c["homebrew"]["level"] != "ok":
        add("Homebrew is how cmux setup installs zig and friends", "install Homebrew from https://brew.sh", "human (admin password)")
    if not pre["tailscale"].get("installed"):
        add("remote access", "install Tailscale and log in to the tailnet", "human")
    elif not pre["tailscale"].get("running"):
        add("remote access", "open Tailscale and log in", "human")
    for a in actions:
        if a["kind"] == "gitpkg" and a["state"] in {"blocked", "failed"}:
            add(f"git {'.'.join(map(str, MIN_GIT))}+ (git maintenance memory bug)", a["note"], "Homebrew owner or operator")
    if any(a["kind"] == "python" and a["state"] in {"blocked", "failed"} for a in actions):
        add("glaeda-mini-enroll needs Python 3.13+ (os.waitid)", enroll_module().PYTHON_FIX,
            "Homebrew owner or operator")
    if c["workloadToolPath"]["level"] != "ok":
        add("cmux build tools must be on the fixed workload PATH", "cd <cmux> && ./scripts/setup.sh", "operator")
    if fleet_result is None:
        add("fleet enrollment verdict", "rerun with --cmux-root <cmux checkout> once cmux ./scripts/setup.sh has run", "operator")
    elif fleet_result.get("eligibleForEnrollment"):
        add("enroll and accept this mini as a fleet node",
            "scripts/glaeda-mini-enroll --cmux-root <cmux checkout> --node-id <cmux-mac-NNN> --apply", "operator")
    root_copy = Path(LAN_FETCH_ROOT_COPY)
    want = hashlib.sha256((SCRIPT_DIR / "glaeda-lan-fetch").read_bytes()).hexdigest()
    try:
        info = root_copy.lstat()
        current = hashlib.sha256(root_copy.read_bytes()).hexdigest() if stat.S_ISREG(info.st_mode) else ""
    except OSError:
        current = ""
    if current != want or not root_chain(root_copy):
        add("cmux CI fetches compiled products from LAN peers through a root-owned glaeda-lan-fetch in a "
            "root-owned directory chain (cmux refuses anything a job could rewrite or rename)",
            f"scripts/glaeda-seed-lan helper-install {platform.node().split('.')[0] or 'HOST'} --apply",
            "operator Mac, then root from a non-cmux admin account or the console, as it prints "
            "(docs/CMUX_MINI_RUNNER.md 2j); never sudo through the cmux account")
    add("Spotlight should skip build output", "System Settings > Spotlight > Search Privacy: add ~/Library/Developer/Xcode/DerivedData", "human (GUI)")
    add("GitHub Actions runner registration (reserved slot, never automated here)",
        "once enrolled: ~/glaeda/scripts/glaeda-cmux-runner --apply (docs/CMUX_MINI_RUNNER.md; routing is glaeda#1174)",
        "org admin + registration token")
    return steps


# What cmux peer_product_source.LAN_FETCH_HELPER runs. Outside /Users/Shared/cmux-build-fleet on purpose: that
# tree is the fleet user's, so a PR job could rename anything in it.
LAN_FETCH_ROOT_COPY = "/Library/Application Support/glaeda/bin/glaeda-lan-fetch"


def root_chain(path: Path) -> bool:
    """PATH and every directory above it are root-owned and not group- or other-writable (cmux's check)."""
    for part in [path, *path.parents]:
        try:
            info = part.lstat()
        except OSError:
            return False
        if info.st_uid != 0 or info.st_mode & 0o022 or stat.S_ISLNK(info.st_mode):
            return False
    return True


def reserved_slots(ctx: Context, fleet_result: dict[str, Any] | None) -> dict[str, Any]:
    return {
        "compilationCacheNode": {
            "state": "reserved",
            "owner": "glaeda RFC #1134 M2 (glaeda node daemon)",
            "note": "gated on the full-app socket-mode measurement; install lands here when M2 ships",
        },
        "runnerRegistration": {
            "state": "not_performed",
            "owner": "cmux docs/ci/mac-fleet.md 3.1-3.2 plus org settings",
            "note": "enrollment makes a routing candidate, not a runner; no token is read or used",
        },
        "fleetEnrollment": fleet_result or {
            "state": "not_run",
            "note": "pass --cmux-root to run scripts/cmux-fleet-bootstrap-macos read-only",
        },
    }


def run_fleet_bootstrap(ctx: Context) -> dict[str, Any] | None:
    if ctx.cmux_root is None:
        return None
    if not ctx.glaeda_bin.is_file():
        return {"state": "not_run", "note": f"glaeda binary missing at {ctx.show(ctx.glaeda_bin)}; see docs/CMUX_FLEET_ENROLLMENT.md"}
    if not ctx.cache_root.is_dir():
        return {"state": "not_run", "note": f"cache root {ctx.show(ctx.cache_root)} does not exist yet; --apply creates it"}
    argv = [sys.executable, os.fspath(SCRIPT_DIR / "cmux_fleet_bootstrap.py"), "--platform", "macos",
            "--cmux-root", os.fspath(ctx.cmux_root), "--glaeda", os.fspath(ctx.glaeda_bin),
            "--cache-root", os.fspath(ctx.cache_root), "--hardware-class", "cmux-mac-build-large",
            "--role", "cmux_macos_native_build"]
    try:
        result = subprocess.run(argv, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=300, check=False)
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as error:
        return {"state": "error", "note": str(error)[:400]}
    if result.returncode != 0:
        try:
            note = json.loads(result.stderr).get("error", "")
        except ValueError:
            note = result.stderr.strip()[-400:]
        return {"state": "refused", "note": note}
    try:
        doc = json.loads(result.stdout)
        if not isinstance(doc, dict):
            raise ValueError("not an object")
    except ValueError:
        return {"state": "unparsed", "note": "bootstrap output was not JSON", "raw": result.stdout[-2000:]}
    return {"state": "observed", "schema": doc.get("schema"),
            "eligibleForEnrollment": doc.get("eligibleForEnrollment"),
            "blockingChecks": doc.get("blockingChecks")}


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- output


def render(ctx: Context, receipt: dict[str, Any]) -> str:
    mode = receipt["mode"]
    lines = [f"glaeda-mini-setup: {mode.upper()}" + ("" if receipt["applied"] else " (nothing changed; add --apply to act)")]
    if ctx.sandbox:
        lines.append(f"  sandbox HOME {ctx.home}: {'systemctl' if ctx.platform == 'linux' else 'launchctl'} is never called")
    pre = receipt["preflight"]
    lines.append("preflight")
    for name, c in pre["checks"].items():
        note = f"  ({c['note']})" if c["note"] and c["level"] != "ok" else ""
        lines.append(f"  {c['level']:<5} {name:<17} {c['value']}{note}")
    lines.append("actions")
    for act in receipt["actions"]:
        target = act.get("label") or (act.get("key") and (act["key"] if act.get("value") is None else f"{act['key']}={act['value']}")) or ctx.show(act.get("path", ""))
        note = f"  ({act['note']})" if act.get("note") else ""
        lines.append(f"  {act['state']:<9} {act['kind']:<6} {target}{note}")
    if receipt["operatorSteps"]:
        lines.append("operator steps (need sudo or a human; this command does not run them)")
    for i, step in enumerate(receipt["operatorSteps"], 1):
        lines.append(f"  {i}. [{step['needs']}] {step['command']}")
        lines.append(f"     {step['why']}")
    if receipt["reserved"]:
        lines.append("reserved slots")
    for name, slot in receipt["reserved"].items():
        extra = ""
        if slot.get("state") == "observed":
            extra = f" eligible={slot['eligibleForEnrollment']} blocking={','.join(slot['blockingChecks']) or 'none'}"
        lines.append(f"  {name}: {slot['state']}{extra}  {slot.get('note', '')}".rstrip())
    lines.append("ready: " + ("yes" if receipt["ready"] else "no, blocking: " + ", ".join(receipt["blocking"])))
    if receipt["applied"]:
        written = ctx.state / "uninstall-receipt.json" if mode == "uninstall" else ctx.receipt_path
        lines.append(f"receipt: {ctx.show(written)}")
    return "\n".join(lines)


def parser() -> argparse.ArgumentParser:
    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="glaeda-mini-setup", description=__doc__,
                                formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    p.add_argument("--apply", action="store_true", help="make the changes (default is plan only)")
    p.add_argument("--uninstall", action="store_true", help="remove what --apply installed")
    p.add_argument("--output", choices=("human", "json"), default="human")
    p.add_argument("--cmux-root", type=Path, help="cmux checkout for the read-only fleet bootstrap")
    p.add_argument("--glaeda", type=Path, help="glaeda binary for the fleet bootstrap "
                   "(default ~/.local/share/glaeda/cmux-fleet/glaeda)")
    p.add_argument("--reclaim-binary", type=Path, help="prebuilt glaeda-worktree-reclaim instead of cargo build")
    p.add_argument("--python", help="interpreter the glaeda-disk agents run (default: Homebrew python3)")
    p.add_argument("--xcode-app", default=CMUX_XCODE_APP, help=f"pinned Xcode (default {CMUX_XCODE_APP})")
    p.add_argument("--min-free-gib", type=int, default=None,
                   help=f"default: one build slot ({MIN_FREE_GIB} GiB on macOS)")
    p.add_argument("--skip-launchctl", "--skip-systemctl", dest="skip_launchctl", action="store_true",
                   help="write plists or units but do not load, enable or unload them")
    p.add_argument("--ota-ring", choices=OTA_RINGS,
                   help="release ring glaeda-update follows (default stable; set once in ~/.config/glaeda/update.json)")
    p.add_argument("--hygiene-only", action="store_true",
                   help="only the disk and worktree hygiene tools and agents, for any Mac or Linux host")
    return p


def run_runner_mode(argv: list[str]) -> int:
    """--runner: hand everything else to scripts/glaeda-cmux-runner (same plan/apply/uninstall style)."""
    import importlib.machinery
    import importlib.util

    loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader("glaeda_cmux_runner", os.fspath(SCRIPT_DIR / "glaeda-cmux-runner"))
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_loader("glaeda_cmux_runner", loader)
    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    loader.exec_module(module)
    module.DARWIN_REQUIRED = DARWIN_REQUIRED
    return module.main(argv)


def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:
    argv = list(sys.argv[1:] if argv is None else argv)
    if "--runner" in argv:
        argv.remove("--runner")
        return run_runner_mode(argv)
    args = parser().parse_args(argv)
    if DARWIN_REQUIRED and platform.system() not in {"Darwin", "Linux"}:
        print("glaeda-mini-setup: macOS or Linux only", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    min_free_gib = args.min_free_gib if args.min_free_gib is not None else fleet.default_min_free_gib(HOST_PLATFORM)
    ctx = Context(Path(os.environ.get("HOME") or pwd.getpwuid(os.getuid()).pw_dir), args.apply, args.python,
                  args.skip_launchctl, args.reclaim_binary,
                  args.cmux_root.expanduser().resolve() if args.cmux_root else None,
                  args.glaeda.expanduser() if args.glaeda else None, args.xcode_app, min_free_gib,
                  args.hygiene_only or HOST_PLATFORM == "linux", ota_ring=args.ota_ring)
    pre = preflight(ctx)
    if ctx.hygiene_only:  # build-host checks are reported, not enforced
        checks = {n: ({**c, "level": "warn"} if c["level"] == "block" and n not in HYGIENE_BLOCKING else c)
                  for n, c in pre["checks"].items()}
        pre = {**pre, "checks": checks, "blocking": [n for n in pre["blocking"] if n in HYGIENE_BLOCKING]}
    if args.uninstall:
        actions = plan_uninstall(ctx)
        if args.apply:
            apply_uninstall(ctx, actions)
    else:
        actions = plan_install(ctx)
        if args.apply:
            apply_install(ctx, actions)
    fleet_result = None if args.uninstall or ctx.hygiene_only else run_fleet_bootstrap(ctx)
    # a failed git install is reported (receipt, operator step) but does not fail the run: glaeda-update
    # rolls a release back when setup fails, and a transient brew error is not the release's fault
    failed = [a for a in actions if a.get("state") == "failed" and a.get("kind") != "gitpkg"]
    receipt = {
        "schema": SCHEMA,
        "mode": "uninstall" if args.uninstall else "install",
        "profile": "hygiene" if ctx.hygiene_only else "build-host",
        "platform": ctx.platform,
        "applied": args.apply,
        "at": datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec="seconds"),
        "sourceRevision": git_revision(),
        "sandboxHome": ctx.sandbox,
        "preflight": pre,
        "actions": actions,
        "operatorSteps": [] if args.uninstall or ctx.hygiene_only else operator_steps(ctx, pre, fleet_result, actions),
        "reserved": {} if args.uninstall or ctx.hygiene_only else reserved_slots(ctx, fleet_result),
        "blocking": pre["blocking"] + [f"action:{a.get('path') or a.get('key')}" for a in actions if a.get("state") in {"blocked", "failed"}],
    }
    receipt["ready"] = not receipt["blocking"]
    if args.apply:
        ctx.state.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True, mode=0o700)
        data = (json.dumps(receipt, indent=2, sort_keys=True) + "\n").encode()
        if args.uninstall:
            # Keep the install receipt readable for a later re-run; record the uninstall beside it.
            write_atomic(ctx.state / "uninstall-receipt.json", data, 0o600)
            if ctx.receipt_path.exists():
                os.replace(ctx.receipt_path, ctx.state / "receipt.uninstalled.json")
        else:
            write_atomic(ctx.receipt_path, data, 0o600)
    if args.output == "json":
        print(json.dumps(receipt, indent=2, sort_keys=True))
    else:
        print(render(ctx, receipt))
    return 1 if failed else 0


def git_revision() -> str | None:
    code, out = run(["git", "-C", os.fspath(REPO), "rev-parse", "HEAD"])
    return out if code == 0 and re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-f]{40}", out) else None


if __name__ == "__main__":
    raise SystemExit(main())
